    long: "Precision is the fraction of positive results that are true positives. Recall is the fraction of real cases the tool catches. The two pull against each other: loosening a rule catches more and raises more false alarms. MITRE's Summiting the Pyramid work describes precision as how well a detection signal can distinguish malicious from benign activity. When the real event is rare, even an accurate rule produces mostly false alarms, so precision depends on the base rate as well as on the rule. For findings sent to engineers, the practical measure is the share they agree are real and worth fixing.",
